{"event_id":"E20000811-1101398","name":null,"merged":false,"episodes":["1101398"],"episode_declared":true,"begin":"2000-08-11 18:10:00","end":"2000-08-12 06:12:00","year":2000,"hazards":["flash-flooding"],"places":["BX","QN"],"harbor":false,"narrative":"Slow moving thunderstorms produced rainfall rates estimated at around 2 inches per hour, which caused significant flooding of low-lying and poor drainage areas.In Huntington, significant flooding occurred along parts of Route 25 and Melville Road.In Yorktown Heights, serious flooding was reported on Commerce Street and Route 118.In Putnam Valley, flooding occurred on Peekskill Hollow Road.In Rockland County, significant flooding caused the closure of many roads in several locations throughout the county.In Pelham Manor, flooding occurred along parts of the Hutchinson River Parkway near Lincoln Avenue.In the Bronx, cars were submerged in rising water and trapped many people.In Bayville, water quickly ponded and rose up to 3 feet, which caused a road closure near the Tide Motel.  Nassau County Police reported severe flooding near the town beach.  NWS radar estimated a 2 to 3 inch rainfall from 2:30 am to 3:30 am, with up to 5 inches during the preceding 24 hours.In Howard Beach (just west of JFK Airport), water quickly ponded and rose up to 2 feet on Cross Bay Blvd. at the Belt Parkway.  The Automated Surface Observing System at JFK Airport measured 1.53 inches.","narrative_damaged":0,"deaths_direct":{"v":0,"s":"ok","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"deaths_indirect":{"v":0,"s":"ok","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"injuries_direct":{"v":0,"s":"ok","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"damage_property":{"v":null,"s":"missing","u":"$","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"damage_crops":{"v":null,"s":"missing","u":"$","src":"ncei-storm-events"},"weather":{"temp_max":{"v":82.0,"s":"ok","u":"F","src":"ghcn-daily","n":"John F. Kennedy Airport, 2000-08-11"},"temp_min":{"v":63.0,"s":"ok","u":"F","src":"ghcn-daily","n":"Newark Liberty Airport, 2000-08-12"},"r